# Vulnerabilities deliberately accepted, with the reason and a date to revisit.
#
# Only advisories that cannot be acted on belong here. Anything with a released
# fix should be fixed instead — `trivy fs --scanners vuln --severity CRITICAL,HIGH .`
# lists them, and CI already passes --ignore-unfixed so unpatched advisories do
# not need an entry unless they warrant a note.
#
# Format: one CVE per line. `exp:` sets an expiry, after which trivy reports it
# again — so an entry cannot quietly become permanent.

# image-size 0.7.5, reached through the documentation toolchain rather than any
# code path this application runs. No fixed version has been released upstream.
# Revisit when one is, or when the dependency that pulls it in is replaced.
CVE-2025-71329 exp:2026-11-30
